  "slug": "decoding-pathology-17b5",
  "summary": "Several preprints infer molecular state from H&E or spot-level spatial data, adding per-prediction confidence and correction for transcript contamination.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational recovery of single-cell molecular state from tissue measurements. Four preprints treat H&E as a molecular readout. Loki2, trained on 15 million cells, tests how much molecular and cellular state routine histology encodes. GenVinci reconstructs 3D molecular tissue scenes and maps senescence across aging mouse organs and human skin. sc-HistoMorphomics links 194 nuclear morphometric features to spatial transcriptomics. REGAIN attaches per-prediction confidence to histology-inferred expression for prognostic analysis in TCGA-BRCA. A second strand improves the reliability of spatial data. st2sc infers single-cell expression from multicellular spots. Dancer separates within-cell-type heterogeneity from transcript contamination. SpaceMACE refines tumour calls using spatial proximity. CIRCA recovers identifiable cell and niche programs tied to plaque pathology. A third strand covers representation learning across modalities: Bloom for brain RNA and chromatin, scUNVEIL with next-UMI pretraining on about 92 million cells, scPACE for donor-level states, and GatorAnchor and Elflow for multi-omics and cytometry. A 3D facial-scan diagnostic benchmark falls outside this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
